## Summary

**Extracted testable command routing from `dispatch.rs` and added comprehensive tests.**

### What changed:

1. `CommandRoute` enum (92 variants) — A pure data type representing which command category an input maps to, with no side effects.

2. `route_command()` function — Pure synchronous routing logic extracted from the pattern-matching in dispatch_command. Handles:
   • Exact matches (/quit, /version, /clear!, etc.)
   • Prefix matches (/model sonnet, /diff --staged, etc.)
   • Special cases (!cmd → Run, `/lint fix → LintFix vs /lint strict` → Lint, /config show|edit|set|get subcommands)
   • UnknownSlash for unrecognized / commands
   • NotACommand for non-slash input

3. `dispatch_command()` refactored — Now `match route_command(ctx.input)` instead of raw string patterns. All handler logic preserved identically.

4. **18 test functions** covering every route category — quit, help, info, model, provider, think, clear, session, git, lint/test, search/nav, config subcommands, file commands, refactoring, memory, conversations, workflow, display, marks, miscellaneous, and edge cases (unknown commands, non-commands, bang prefix).

